<div class="bt">
  <h1>Likutay Halachos</h1>
  <div class="vol">Orach Chaim — Volume 3</div>
</div>

<div class="hh">
  <h2>Hilchos Pesach</h2>
  <span class="hd"></span>
</div>

<div class="hs">
Continuation of Hilchos Rosh Chodesh 3 — Based on Likutay Moharan I, Torah 56:<br>
<em>"Uv'yom habikurim — l'ha'arich yamim al mamlachto"</em><br>
<em>This is the aspect of Shabbos HaGadol — the Shabbos before Pesach</em>
</div>

<div class="sl">
Sections 1–11 · Plus addenda pertaining to Rosh Chodesh and Sefirah
</div>


<!-- ══════════ Section 1 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 1 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
For the <span class="kt">Exodus from Egypt</span>, which is the aspect of the <span class="kt">revelation of the concealment</span>, depends on <span class="kt">Shabbos</span>, as mentioned above. For the <span class="kt">Pesach offering in Egypt</span> was taken on the tenth [of Nissan] and required <span class="kt">four days of inspection</span>, so that Yisrael would be occupied with mitzvos for four days. "Four days" specifically — so that they could reveal the concealment to elevate <em>Malchus</em>, which is the aspect of <span class="kt">four camps</span>, as mentioned above. Therefore, at the time of the first Pesach when they went out of Egypt, the <span class="kt">beginning was on Shabbos</span>. For specifically on Shabbos the redemption from Egypt begins, because from there one receives the <em>daas</em> to reveal the <em>Malchus</em>, which is the aspect of the number four, from within the concealment, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, what was established for all generations is only the <span class="kt">Shabbos before Pesach</span> and not the tenth of the month — for the essential miracle depends on the Shabbos before Pesach, as mentioned above. And this is why it is called <span class="kt">Shabbos HaGadol</span> — that is, Shabbos is "great," greater than all the other days and times, for they all receive their holiness from it, as mentioned above. And because this particular Shabbos reveals this — since we saw the redemption from Egypt that came about through it — therefore it is called Shabbos HaGadol, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, in <span class="kt">Nissan</span>, in which the redemption from Egypt took place — which is the aspect of <em>Kiddush HaChodesh</em>, the aspect of Rosh Chodesh — therefore it is called <span class="kt"><em>Rosh Chadashim</em></span> (the head of months), as it is written <span class="vs">(Shemos 12:2)</span>: <span class="v">"This month shall be for you the head of months."</span> That is: Nissan, the entire month, is in the aspect of Rosh Chodesh — for in it the redemption from Egypt took place, which is the aspect of Rosh Chodesh, as mentioned above. Therefore, the <span class="kt">twelve <em>N'si'im</em></span> (princes) of the twelve tribes of Hashem brought their offerings in it — corresponding to the <span class="kt">twelve months of the year</span>, which are the aspect of the completeness of the holy <em>Malchus</em> that stands upon the twelve oxen, as mentioned above. For Nissan comprises them all, since in it the holy <em>Malchus</em> was revealed in the aspect of the Exodus from Egypt, which is the aspect of the holiness of Rosh Chodesh. Therefore, they all depend on it and it comprises them all. Therefore, the <span class="kt">entire month is treated as a Yom Tov</span> and we do not say <em>Tachanun</em> in it — for the entire month is in the aspect of Rosh Chodesh, since in it the aspect of the holiness of Rosh Chodesh was revealed, as mentioned above.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 2 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 2 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And this is that when Yisrael went out of Egypt and the concealment was revealed as mentioned above, they merited <span class="kt"><em>matzah</em></span>, which is the aspect of exceedingly great <em>daas</em>, in the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em></span> (dispute for the sake of Heaven), as is brought there in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span> mentioned above. For through the revelation of the concealment, exceedingly great <em>daas</em> was drawn in the aspect of <em>matzah</em>, which is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt">transformation from <em>chametz</em> to <em>matzah</em></span> — that they emerged from the aspect of <em>chametz</em> and merited <em>matzah</em>. For there is only a <span class="kt">hairsbreadth between <em>chametz</em> and <em>matzah</em></span> — that is, between the <em>Ches</em> and the <em>Hei</em>, as is found in the Holy Zohar: <span class="sq">"Break the leg of the <em>Ches</em> and make of it a <em>Hei</em>"</span> — on the verse <span class="v">"Rebuke the beast of the reed"</span> <span class="vs">(Tehillim 68:31)</span>. That is: to break the leg of the <em>Ches</em> of <em>chametz</em>, and then <em>chametz</em> becomes <em>matzah</em>; see there.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt">breaking the concealment</span> — that one breaks the concealment and opens a passageway in it and reveals the <em>daas</em>. And then the concealment is transformed into <em>daas</em> — from <em>chametz</em> to <em>matzah</em>. For <em>chametz</em> is <span class="sq"><em>tukpa d'dina</em></span> (the force of strict judgment), the aspect of the hiding of the Face, the aspect of <span class="kt">"Pharaoh"</span> which is <span class="kt">"the back of the neck" (<em>ha'oref</em>)</span>, the aspect of the wicked kingdom — which is the leg of the <em>Ches</em> of <em>chametz</em>, in the aspect of <span class="v">"the beast of the reed, the congregation of the mighty"</span>, which alludes to the <em>Ches</em> of <em>chametz</em>, as mentioned above. And one must break the leg of the <em>Ches</em> mentioned above — in the aspect of breaking the concealment — and open a passageway in it to reveal and show the <em>daas</em> enclothed there: that, as it were, even there His G-dliness, blessed be He, is found, and <span class="v">"His Kingship rules over all."</span> And then <em>chametz</em> is transformed into <em>matzah</em>, for the concealment is transformed into <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 3 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 3 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And this is why we take <span class="kt">three <em>matzos</em></span> and <span class="kt">break the middle one</span> into two — and then they become <span class="kt">four</span>. That is: even within the <em>matzah</em> itself, which is the side of holiness, we allude to the aspect of <span class="kt">breaking the concealment</span>. For the essential sustenance of the aspect of concealment is from the <span class="kt"><em>raglayim</em></span> (feet), from the aspect of the <span class="kt">fourth camp</span>, which is the <span class="kt">camp of Dan</span>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, at first there are only <span class="kt">three <em>matzos</em></span> — this is the aspect of before the revelation of the concealment, when it is only in the aspect of the three camps, as mentioned above. And afterward, we break the middle one into two — which is the aspect of an allusion to the breaking of the concealment. And then, from three, <span class="kt">four</span> are made — for now the <em>Malchus</em> is completed in the aspect of four camps, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, we break the <span class="kt">middle one</span>, which is the <span class="kt">Levi</span> — from whom judgments are aroused, as is known. And from there the sustenance of the concealment cascades down. One must <span class="kt">sweeten the judgment at its root</span>, and then of their own accord they are broken and fall below. And this is the aspect of breaking the middle <em>matzah</em>, which is the Levi — to break and sweeten the power of the judgments within holiness. This is the aspect of the <span class="kt">Exodus from the supernal Egypt</span> — from the <span class="kt">narrow passage of the throat</span> (<em>meitzar hagaron</em>), which is the side of Levi, as is known. And through this, of its own accord, the concealment and the <em>Sitra Achra</em> below are broken. And then the <em>daas</em> is revealed, and then the <em>Malchus</em> is completed in the aspect of four camps. Therefore, from three <em>matzos</em>, four are now made, as mentioned above.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 4 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 4 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
Therefore, the essential mitzvah of <em>matzah</em> is specifically with the one that was <span class="kt">broken</span> — with which we fulfill the eating of <em>matzah</em> and the <span class="kt"><em>Afikoman</em></span>. And it is called <span class="kt"><em>lechem oni</em></span> (bread of affliction/poverty), which is the essential <em>matzah</em>, as is brought. For specifically through the aspect of breaking the middle <em>matzah</em>, the aspect of <em>matzah</em> is formed — for it is itself the aspect of breaking <em>chametz</em> into <em>matzah</em>, that is, the aspect of the revelation of the concealment, which is accomplished through breaking the aspect of the Levi, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore it is called <span class="kt"><em>Yachatz</em></span> — in the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>chatzos</em></span> (midnight), in the aspect of <span class="v">"At about midnight, I will go out in the midst of Egypt"</span> — the aspect of the revelation of the concealment, as mentioned above. And this is done <span class="kt">after <em>Kiddush</em></span>. For <em>Kiddush</em> is the aspect of <em>mikra kodesh</em> — that one calls the holy, the wisdom and <em>daas</em> which is the vitality, as mentioned above. And through this the day is sanctified. And therefore, through this <em>daas</em>, one can reveal the concealment as mentioned above — and this is the aspect of <em>Yachatz</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 5 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 5 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And <span class="sq">"here the son asks"</span> — after the middle <em>matzah</em> has been broken, that is, the Levi, and the <em>daas</em> has been revealed from the concealment (from which the aspect of <em>matzah</em> itself is formed, as mentioned above) — therefore, then the <span class="kt">son asks questions</span> and poses difficulties: <span class="v">"<em>Mah nishtanah</em> — What is different..."</span> etc. This is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>machlokes</em></span> (dispute) — questions and difficulties that arouse the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, which is the completeness of <em>daas</em> in the fullest sense, the aspect of <em>matzah</em> — which is a term for <span class="kt">contention and strife</span>, as is explained there.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, <span class="sq">"here the son asks"</span> — <span class="kt">"the son"</span> specifically — that is, questions and difficulties in the aspect of <em>machlokes</em> that are aroused between the <span class="kt">son and the father</span>. This is the aspect of <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, the <span class="kt"><em>machlokes</em> of Shammai and Hillel</span>, which is exceedingly great <em>daas</em> and the sustenance of the world. For the essential creation and sustenance of the world is through the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness — that is, the aspect of the <span class="kt">initial <em>tzimtzum</em></span> (contraction), when, as it were, the light was contracted and divided to the sides. For without this there would have been no space for creation, as is known.
</p>

<p class="p">
And creation and before-creation are in the aspect of <span class="kt">father and son</span>, as Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote. And there must necessarily be a <em>machlokes</em> between them, as it were — that after creation there should be some division from before creation; for otherwise creation would be nullified, as mentioned above. Nevertheless, in truth, there is the <span class="kt">ultimate unity</span> there, and this aspect of <em>machlokes</em> that is in truth the ultimate peace — this is impossible to grasp, for there at the beginning of the <em>tzimtzum</em>, there is no comprehension and it is forbidden to investigate there, for it is the <span class="v">"ways of Hashem"</span> and <span class="sq">"into what is beyond you, do not inquire"</span>.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is itself the aspect of the <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em> between the true Tzadikim and sages — the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> of Shammai and Hillel — which is the sustenance of the world: so that there be space for creation. That is, their dispute is in the aspect of the <span class="kt">division of the light to the sides</span> so that there be the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>chalal hapanui</em></span> (empty space), so that there be space for creation, as Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote in the discourse <span class="v">"Bo el Pharaoh"</span> <span class="vs">(Siman 64)</span>, on the Mishnah <span class="sq">"All my days I grew up among the sages"</span>; see there well.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> and questioning of the <span class="kt">son to the father</span> — the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> of Shammai and Hillel, which is the sustenance of the world, as mentioned above. And this is needed now, on <span class="kt">the night of Pesach</span>, when there is the aspect of the <span class="kt">renewal of the world</span>, as is brought. That is: the essential aspect of the concealment — which is the sustenance of the <em>Sitra Achra</em> — is from the aspect of the shattering of vessels that comes from an excess of light, as mentioned above. And then, in Egypt, they reached the ultimate descent until the world nearly returned, <em>chas v'shalom</em>, to <span class="kt"><em>tohu vavohu</em></span> (chaos and void). Therefore, they needed to return and <span class="kt">rectify the world anew</span> through the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, which is the aspect of the initial <em>tzimtzum</em> within holiness — to draw the light in measure — and this is the essential sustenance of the world, as mentioned above. And this is the essential completeness of holiness and the revelation of <em>Malchus</em> — <span class="sq"><em>b'gin d'yishtamud'un laih</em></span>, "in order that they should know Him," for <span class="sq">"there is no king without a people"</span>.
</p>

<p class="p">
And when there is no <em>machlokes</em> within holiness — which is the aspect of the initial <em>tzimtzum</em> — there is no space for creation and no one to know of His Kingship, blessed be He, as it were. Therefore, the essential completeness of the holy <em>Malchus</em> is through the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, as mentioned above. And therefore, we make <span class="kt">changes on the night of Pesach</span>, so that the son should ask <em>"Mah nishtanah"</em> — to arouse the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And then we tell the <span class="kt">Haggadah</span>. For to merit <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em> is through a <span class="kt">sigh</span> (<em>anachah</em>), through which the <span class="kt">melancholy — the contamination of the Serpent</span> — is subdued; see there. That is: one needs teshuvah and sighing afterward to rectify and subdue the <em>Sitra Achra</em>, the contamination of the Serpent, so that they should not grasp hold of the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness mentioned above. For this is what Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote there — that one must <span class="kt">purify and cleanse the heavens</span>, that is, the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, which is fire and water — so that it should not be in the aspect of <span class="v">"the heavens are clothed in darkness"</span>. That is, so that they should not grasp hold there, <em>chas v'shalom</em>. For the <em>machlokes</em>, even though it is within holiness and is supernal <em>daas</em> and completeness of holiness — nevertheless, from there it cascades downward until they gain a grip from there, as is known. For the <em>Sitra Achra</em> is the aspect of <em>machlokes</em>, and its sustenance is from the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness. Therefore, one must guard and purify the heavens — the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness — and this is through sighing and teshuvah, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt">telling of the Haggadah</span>, in which we mention the <span class="kt">sighs and cries</span> that we experienced then, as it is written <span class="vs">(Shemos 2:23)</span>: <span class="v">"And we cried out to Hashem... and the children of Yisrael sighed,"</span> etc. And similarly, this is done in every generation, as is known. And through this, the <span class="kt">heavens are purified</span> — that is, the hands — and then one merits to receive <span class="kt">speech from the hands</span>, which is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as is explained; see there well.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt">Pesach, <em>matzah</em>, and <em>maror</em></span>. That we eat <em>matzah</em> and <em>maror</em> afterward — this is the aspect of <span class="kt">fire and water, <em>chesed</em> and <em>g'vurah</em>, right hand and left hand, Hillel and Shammai</span> — the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as mentioned above. And afterward they would eat the <span class="kt">Pesach offering</span>, as it is written <span class="vs">(Bamidbar 9:11)</span>: <span class="v">"Upon <em>matzos</em> and bitter herbs shall they eat it."</span> <em>Pesach</em> is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>peh sach</em></span> — "a mouth that speaks" — the aspect of the <span class="kt">speech that one receives from the hands</span> mentioned above, in the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, <span class="kt">Hillel</span> would <span class="kt">wrap them together</span> — to show that in truth, <span class="sq">"these and these are the words of the living G-d"</span>, and it is a <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, which is great peace and great <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above. Therefore, specifically <span class="kt">Hillel</span> would do this — for he is the one involved in the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, the aspect of the <em>machlokes</em> of Shammai and Hillel, as mentioned above. And in truth, there was great peace between them, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="sq">"They did not refrain from one another"</span> etc. — <span class="sq">"to make known that there was love and brotherhood between them."</span> Therefore, this <em>machlokes</em> within holiness has a <span class="kt">resolution</span>, as is known. And the resolution is from the side of Hillel — from the side of <em>chesed</em>, as is known. Therefore, specifically Hillel would wrap them together, as mentioned above. And therefore, we make the <span class="kt"><em>Koreich</em></span> (wrapping) with the <span class="kt"><em>Yisrael</em></span> — the third <em>matzah</em> — for there the resolution is, as is known.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 6 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 6 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And afterward we eat the <span class="kt"><em>Afikoman</em></span>. It is called <span class="kt"><em>Tzafun</em></span> (hidden) in the order of the Haggadah. This is the aspect of the <span class="kt">cake they brought out of Egypt</span> — they tasted in it the <span class="kt">taste of <em>man</em></span> (manna). "That they <em>brought out</em>" specifically — for after they went out and the <em>daas</em> was revealed, which is the aspect of <em>matzah</em>, then they tasted in it the taste of <em>man</em>. That is: the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, which is in truth peace and great <em>daas</em>, the aspect of <em>man</em>, as is explained there; see there well.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>Afikoman</em></span> — <span class="sq"><em>afiku man</em></span> — "bring out the manna!" — the aspect of the <em>matzah</em> that they brought out of Egypt and tasted in it the taste of <em>man</em>, as mentioned above. For now, after all the above, they already merited the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em> as mentioned above, and now the <em>matzah</em> is properly rectified in completeness, in the aspect of <em>man</em>. And this is <span class="sq"><em>afiku man</em></span>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, until now it was <span class="kt">hidden away</span> (<em>tzafun</em>) and concealed — in the aspect of concealment. For although the revelation of the concealment had already been aroused at the beginning, nevertheless it still needed to be hidden and concealed, so that they should not grasp hold, <em>chas v'shalom</em>, of the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, as mentioned above — for the <em>daas</em> had not yet been fully revealed, as mentioned above. But now that the aspect of the <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em> has been completed and revealed as mentioned above, then we bring out the <em>Afikoman</em> — which is the aspect of the cake that they brought out of Egypt, etc., as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">[Note: Pages are missing in the printed editions until the next section.]</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 7 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 7 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt">two hand-washings</span> that are done [at the Seder] — washing the hands twice. For the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness that one receives from the <span class="kt">hands</span>, one must purify the hands, which are the aspect of the <span class="kt">heavens</span>. And this is the aspect of <span class="kt">washing the hands</span> that is done before eating bread specifically — to purify the hands in order to merit that the bread should be in the aspect of <span class="kt">bread from heaven</span>, which is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as is explained there; see there. (And see all this in <span class="vs">Hilchos N'tilas Yadayim</span>.)
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the hand-washing <span class="kt">after the Haggadah</span>, which is the aspect of crying out and sighing — through which one purifies the hands, as is explained there. Therefore, immediately afterward comes <span class="kt"><em>Rachtzah</em></span> — washing and purifying the hands. And then one merits the aspect of <em>matzah</em> and <em>maror</em> and <em>Afikoman</em> — the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, also at the beginning, before breaking the middle <em>matzah</em> — when the beginning of the revelation of the aspect of <em>matzah</em>, the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, occurs as mentioned above — we wash our hands as well, in the aspect of purifying the hands, as mentioned above. And the <span class="kt">two washings</span> are the aspect of <span class="kt">two kinds of purification</span>, the aspect of two kinds of <em>mikva'os</em>: one at the <span class="kt">beginning of the revelation of <em>daas</em></span>, which is the beginning of teshuvah; and one when one merits the <span class="kt">revelation of <em>daas</em> in completeness</span> and teshuvah in completeness and full rectification — which are in the aspect of <span class="kt">Pesach and Shavuos</span>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
For at first, when Yisrael went out of Egypt, they merited the <em>mikveh</em> — that is, <em>daas</em> — for they all immersed then. And afterward, through the counting — which are days of teshuvah in which one goes back and rectifies all the blemishes — afterward one merits great rectification in completeness, which is the aspect of <span class="kt">Shavuos</span>, the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>mikveh</em> of Shavuos</span>, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of the two washings mentioned above. For hand-washing is in the aspect of purification, the aspect of a <em>mikveh</em>: the washing and purification at the beginning of the revelation of <em>daas</em>, the aspect of <em>machlokes</em>, the aspect of <em>matzah</em>; and afterward, when one merits the <em>daas</em> as mentioned above. And the essential purification is in the hands — to purify the aspect of the heavens, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, we do <span class="kt">not recite a blessing on the first washing</span> — for it is not yet complete; it is only the beginning of purification, the beginning of teshuvah through the arousal, as mentioned above. Not until the second time — when the purification and washing are proper and complete, with a blessing, as mentioned above.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 8 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 8 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>Karpas</em></span>, which is the <span class="kt"><em>mochin d'katnus</em></span> (constricted consciousness) from which the judgments draw sustenance — which are the aspect of the hiding of the Face. Through the <em>Kiddush</em>, which is the aspect of <em>mikra kodesh</em> — calling the holy, the vitality and <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above — one can draw <em>chesed</em> and <em>daas</em> to sweeten the aspect of the concealment and reveal it.
</p>

<p class="p">
This is the aspect of the <span class="kt">dipping</span> — dipping the <em>Karpas</em> in salt water — which is the aspect of <span class="kt">sweetening</span>: sweetening the aspect of the concealment, as mentioned above. Therefore, we take a type of <span class="kt">vegetable</span> for <em>Karpas</em>, in the aspect of <span class="sq">"Esther was greenish, and a thread of <em>chesed</em> was drawn upon her"</span>. For Esther is the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> when it is in concealment, in the aspect of <span class="v">"I will surely hide"</span> (<em>haster astir</em>), as Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote there.
</p>

<p class="p">
The dipping of the vegetable alludes to the <span class="kt">thread of <em>chesed</em></span> that is drawn into the aspect of concealment — the aspect of <span class="sq">"Esther was greenish"</span> etc., as mentioned above. Through this, the concealment is revealed and <em>daas</em> is formed from it, the aspect of <em>matzah</em>, as mentioned above. This is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>Karpas</em> — <em>Yachatz</em></span>: through the dipping and sweetening of the <em>Karpas</em> as mentioned above, one reveals the concealment and the aspect of <em>matzah</em> is revealed — which is the aspect of <em>Yachatz</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And when the concealment is revealed and transformed into <em>daas</em>, then the <span class="sq">Torah proclaims before them</span> and they return in teshuvah. Thus, from the <span class="kt">concealment itself</span>, the <span class="kt">arousal of teshuvah</span> is formed, as mentioned above. And this is alluded to by the <span class="kt">vegetable</span> that we take for <em>Karpas</em> — which alludes to <span class="kt">teshuvah</span>, as Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote in the discourse <span class="v">"Ani Hashem hu Sh'mi"</span> <span class="vs">(Siman 11)</span>, on the Midrash where Yochani and Mamrei asked Moshe: <span class="sq">"Are you bringing straw to <em>Afarayim</em>?"</span> And Moshe answered: <span class="sq"><em>"L'masa yarka, yarka sh'kol"</em></span> — "To a city of vegetables, bring vegetables"; see there in the aforementioned discourse. For the <em>yarka</em> (vegetable/green) alludes to teshuvah, in the aspect of <span class="v">"<em>Vayarek</em> es chanichav"</span> <span class="vs">(B'raishis 14:14)</span> — <span class="sq">"he made them green with teshuvah,"</span> as is brought in the Midrash, etc.; see there.
</p>

<p class="p">
And to allude to Moshe's aforementioned answer, we take a vegetable for <em>Karpas</em>. For through the revelation of the concealment, from it comes the arousal of teshuvah, the aspect of <span class="v">"<em>Vayarek</em> es chanichav,"</span> as mentioned above. For through the <em>Karpas</em> — that is, the dipping of the vegetable — great <em>daas</em> is formed in the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>. For the dipping is so that the <span class="kt">children should see and ask</span> <em>"Mah nishtanah,"</em> as our Sages, of blessed memory, said. And the son's question is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, which is the aspect of great <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Thus, through the <em>Karpas</em> — the vegetable — great <em>daas</em> is revealed in the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, the aspect of <em>matzah</em>, as mentioned above. This is the aspect of <span class="kt">teshuvah</span> that is formed through the revelation of <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above. And it is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>teshuvah hamishkal</em></span> (proportionate teshuvah). For the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em> is exceedingly great and lofty <em>daas</em>, and it is revealed specifically from within the <span class="kt">ultimate concealment</span> — for specifically there, exceedingly great <em>daas</em> is enclothed, as mentioned above. Therefore, when one reveals the concealment, specifically from this comes great <em>daas</em>, and it is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt">Moshe's answer</span> mentioned above. For they asked him: "You are bringing straw to <em>Afarayim</em>?" — for Yisrael, when they are on a lowly level, are likened to <span class="kt">dust (<em>afar</em>)</span>. They questioned him for bringing the deep wisdoms of Torah into Yisrael who are on a lowly level, in the aspect of dust. And Moshe answered them: it is an adage among people — that through speaking the <span class="kt">words of Torah with the mouth</span>, it illuminates for them to do <em>teshuvah hamishkal</em>. This is <span class="sq"><em>"l'masa yarka, yarka sh'kol"</em></span> — the aspect of <em>teshuvah hamishkal</em> through all this (Rabeinu, may his light shine, explained all this; see there). That is: they asked him, since they are on such a lowly level, as in the ultimate descent and concealment that existed then in Egypt — it should be enough to raise them from their descent, to lift them from the dust. But it is not fitting to bring them to the deep wisdoms of Torah, which would be going from one extreme to the other. And he answered them: through the Torah, one merits <em>teshuvah hamishkal</em>. Therefore, on the contrary, they specifically need to come to the deep wisdoms of Torah, to the depths, to merit exceedingly great <em>daas</em> — so that their teshuvah will truly be <em>teshuvah hamishkal</em>, and in what they blemished they will rectify. For when they were in the ultimate descent, specifically there, exceedingly great <em>daas</em> was enclothed, as mentioned above. Therefore, one must specifically elevate and reveal this <em>daas</em>. Therefore, one specifically needs to come to exceedingly great <em>daas</em>, which is the aspect of <em>teshuvah hamishkal</em> — and in what they blemished, they will rectify, as mentioned above.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 9 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 9 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
Also, <span class="kt"><em>Karpas</em></span> is a term for <span class="kt">fine cloth</span>, as it is written <span class="vs">(Esther 1:6)</span>: <span class="v">"<em>chur karpas</em> and blue"</span>. It alludes to the <span class="kt"><em>K'sones Passim</em></span> (coat of many colors) that Yaakov made for Yosef — through which things unfolded until our forefathers descended to Egypt (and I believe this is brought in the holy books). For the <em>K'sones Passim</em> is the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>Chaluka d'Rabbanan</em></span> (the garment of the Sages), the aspect of the <span class="kt">Oral Torah</span>, which is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>. For this reason it is called <em>chaluka</em> — a term meaning <span class="kt">differences of opinion</span> (<em>chilukei dei'os</em>).
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, through the <em>K'sones</em> and this garment, the <span class="kt"><em>machlokes</em> between Yosef and his brothers</span> was aroused — for through it, <span class="v">"they hated him"</span> and disputed with him. And this <em>machlokes</em> between Yosef and his brothers ought to have been in the aspect of <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, which is the sustenance of the world. And certainly, their intention was so, for their dispute was certainly intended for the sake of Heaven. However, they were not saved from blemish, and that <em>machlokes</em> within holiness was blemished — until the <em>Sitra Achra</em> drew sustenance from it, for their essential sustenance is from the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness, as mentioned above. And through this, things unfolded and our forefathers descended to Egypt.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, now on <span class="kt">Pesach</span>, at the time of the Exodus from Egypt, we take <span class="kt"><em>Karpas</em></span>, an allusion to the <em>K'sones Passim</em>, as mentioned above. Through this, the child asks <em>"Mah nishtanah"</em> — which is the aspect of <em>machlokes l'shem shamayim</em>, <em>machlokes</em> within holiness. And we rectify what was blemished in the <em>machlokes</em> within holiness — the aspect of the <em>K'sones Passim</em> — by the brothers of Yosef, as mentioned above. (And see the discourse <span class="v">"T'hilah l'Dovid"</span>, <span class="vs">Siman 12</span>, what is explained on the verse <span class="v">"<em>Vayarek</em> es chanichav"</span> — the aspect of the <span class="kt">green line that encircles the world</span>.)
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 10 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 10 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of: on the <span class="kt">night of the fourteenth</span>, we <span class="kt">search for <em>chametz</em> by the light of a candle</span>. "The night of the fourteenth" — for then is the aspect of the revelation of <em>daas</em>, since the illumination of the <span class="kt">thirteen days</span> from Rosh Chodesh until now has already been drawn. These are the aspect of great <em>daas</em> and great mercy, in the aspect of an <span class="kt">elder with settled <em>daas</em></span> — the aspect of the <span class="kt">fourteen rectifications of the beard</span> (<em>Tikuna DiY'kana</em>). Through this <em>daas</em>, one can reveal the concealment as mentioned above — and this is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>bi'ur chametz</em></span> (the destruction of <em>chametz</em>), to destroy the <em>chametz</em> and the concealment and reveal the <em>daas</em> in the aspect of <em>matzah</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, specifically on the <span class="kt">night of the fourteenth</span> we search for <em>chametz</em> — for through the completeness of the <em>daas</em> of the aspect of the thirteen, as mentioned above, one can search the <em>chametz</em> and destroy it and reveal the concealment, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt">"by the light of a candle."</span> And our Sages, of blessed memory, derived that the light of a candle is effective for searching, from the verse <span class="vs">(Mishlai 20:27)</span>: <span class="v">"The candle of Hashem is the soul of man, searching all the chambers of the belly."</span> That is: through the light of the candle — the <em>daas</em>, which is the aspect of <span class="v">"the candle of Hashem is the soul of man"</span>, as it is written <span class="vs">(Iyov 32:8)</span>: <span class="v">"And the breath of the Almighty gives them understanding"</span> — through this, it is effective to search the <em>chametz</em>, to reveal the concealment and destroy the wickedness and the <em>Sitra Achra</em>, to return the wicked in teshuvah, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt">searching for <em>chametz</em> in the holes and cracks</span> and all the places that cannot be easily seen — but through the light of the candle, they are searched. For through the aspect of the light of the candle — the <em>daas</em> — one can reprove and warn and bring back in teshuvah even one in whom the <em>chametz</em> and wickedness have become so deeply embedded that it is not visible at all, in the aspect of <span class="sq">"one who transgresses and repeats it — it becomes to him as if it were permitted"</span> — and even worse, <em>chas v'shalom</em>, in the aspect of <span class="kt">concealment within concealment</span>, as is explained there in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span> mentioned above. And through the <em>daas</em>, the aspect of the light of the candle, one can search and destroy the wickedness even from such places — for one can bring back in teshuvah even one who is in the aspect of concealment within concealment, through the <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And therefore it is called <span class="kt"><em>"or l'arba'ah asar"</em></span> — "the <span class="kt">light</span> of the fourteenth." And our Sages, of blessed memory, said that the night is called "light" on account of the verse <span class="vs">(Tehillim 148:3)</span>: <span class="v">"Praise Him, all you stars of light."</span> That is: the aspect of <span class="v">"those who bring the many to righteousness are like the stars"</span> <span class="vs">(Daniel 12:3)</span> — they who bring people back in teshuvah are called <span class="sq">"those who bring the many to righteousness."</span> And since they illuminate specifically in the aspect of the <span class="kt">night</span> — within the darkness and night, the aspect of concealment — specifically there they illuminate the light of their <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above, in order to illuminate the night and reveal the concealment, as mentioned above. For specifically there, great light is enclothed, as mentioned above. And for this reason the night is called <span class="kt">"light"</span> — the aspect of <span class="sq"><em>"or l'arba'ah asar"</em></span>, we search, etc. — the aspect of the revelation of the concealment, returning the wicked in teshuvah — the aspect of <span class="v">"those who bring the many to righteousness like the stars"</span> — the aspect of <span class="v">"stars of <em>light</em>."</span> And for this reason they called this night specifically <span class="kt">"light,"</span> as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, we search for <em>chametz</em> specifically <span class="kt">at night</span>. For specifically in the aspect of the night — in the aspect of the darkness and concealment to the utmost degree — specifically then, one reveals it through the light of <em>daas</em>, which is the aspect of <span class="kt">the light of the candle</span>.
</p>


<!-- ══════════ Section 11 ══════════ -->
<div class="sn"><span>— 11 —</span></div>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>Sefiras HaOmer</em></span> (the counting of the <em>Omer</em>). The mitzvah is to <span class="kt">count the days</span>, in order to purify us from our impurity — to count, specifically. So that the days should be <span class="kt">numbered and counted</span>, that they should be <span class="kt">divided and measured</span>, each one on its own — so that they should be in the aspect of <span class="kt">vessels — days and attributes</span> — to receive the light <span class="kt">in measure</span>, in the aspect of <span class="v">"the measure of my days, what is it?"</span> — so that there should not be an excess of light causing etc., as is understood there in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span>. For this is the essential aspect of the <span class="kt">Torah</span>, which is the <em>Sh'ma d'Kudsha B'rich Hu</em> — the aspect of <span class="kt">vessels and attributes</span> to receive the light, so that an excess of oil should not cause the extinguishing of the lamp.
</p>

<p class="p">
And through this specifically, one reveals the concealment. For the concealment is the aspect of the grip of the wicked kingdom, whose sustenance is from the shattering of vessels, which come about through an excess of light, as mentioned above. Thus, the essential rectification is to make <span class="kt">vessels and attributes</span> to receive the light in measure — and this is the greatness of the Torah, as mentioned above, which is the aspect of <span class="v">"the measure of my days, what is it?"</span> as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, one must count <em>Sefiras HaOmer</em> — to count the days specifically — so that they should be numbered and measured, the aspect of <span class="v">"the measure of my days"</span> etc. — to receive the light in measure, which is the essential rectification. And therefore, the <span class="kt">counting purifies us from our impurity</span>. For the essential grip of impurity is from the aspect of the shattering of vessels that comes through an excess of light, as mentioned above. Therefore, the essential purification and rectification is through the <span class="kt">vessels and attributes</span>, which is the aspect of the counting, the aspect of <span class="v">"the measure of my days"</span> — that one counts the days so that they are counted and measured, so that one should not enter the boundary of another, so that they should not be mixed together — so that it should not be in the aspect of the shattering of vessels, which is the shattering of the days when they are mixed together. Rather, they should be in the aspect of the rectification — each and every one a vessel and attribute on its own, each one counted on its own, to receive the light in measure. And this is the aspect of the counting, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
For the counting is for the sake of <span class="kt">the receiving of the Torah</span>. For the Exodus from Egypt on Pesach, although it was the aspect of the revelation of the concealment as mentioned above, nevertheless it was not yet in complete perfection — because they had not yet received the Torah, as is brought. For the essential revelation of the concealment is through the Torah, as mentioned above. And the essential completeness of the revelation of the holy <em>Malchus</em> is on <span class="kt">Shavuos</span>, through the Torah.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, beforehand, the counting was needed — which is a <span class="kt">preparation for receiving the Torah</span>. That is: one counts and measures the days, in the aspect of <span class="v">"the measure of my days, what is it?"</span> — to receive the light in measure, which is the essential greatness of the Torah that is received on Shavuos — which is the aspect of the <em>Sh'ma d'Kudsha B'rich Hu</em>, the aspect of days and attributes, the aspect of <span class="v">"the measure of my days, what is it?"</span> as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, we count <span class="kt">seven weeks</span>, corresponding to the <span class="kt">seven days</span> — to rectify all seven days so that they should be in the aspect of vessels and attributes, as mentioned above. For also at the <span class="kt">beginning of creation</span>, the essential rectification of creation was through this aspect: that each day was measured and numbered on its own. And this is what is written in the account of creation: <span class="v">"And it was evening, and it was morning — day one"</span> — and so for each day. And this is the aspect of the counting — that each day is numbered on its own, so that it should be in the aspect of attributes and vessels, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And the entire creation was <span class="kt">suspended until the day of the Giving of the Torah</span>, which is the sixth of Sivan, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said. Therefore, before the Giving of the Torah, one also needs to count the days — for this is the rectification of creation, as mentioned above. And one must count specifically <span class="kt">seven weeks</span>, for in them there are <span class="kt">seven Shabbasos</span>. And the essential rectification of the counting — which is the aspect of the rectification of the revelation of the concealment — is through <span class="kt">Shabbos</span>, which is <em>daas</em>, as mentioned above. Therefore, seven Shabbasos are needed to rectify all seven days through seven Shabbasos. And this is what is written <span class="vs">(Vayikra 23:15)</span>: <span class="v">"Seven Shabbasos, complete shall they be."</span> For the essential rectification is through seven Shabbasos, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is what is written <span class="vs">(Vayikra 23:15)</span>: <span class="v">"And you shall count for yourselves from the morrow of the Shabbos."</span> And our Sages, of blessed memory, said that <span class="kt">Yom Tov is also called Shabbos</span>. For Yom Tov is called Shabbos because all the holiness of Yom Tov is drawn through Shabbos, as mentioned above. And for this same reason, Shabbos is mentioned in connection with the counting — for also the rectification of the counting, that is, to reveal the concealment, is drawn from Shabbos, as mentioned above — which is itself what Yom Tov receives from Shabbos, which is the revelation of the concealment as well, as mentioned above.
</p>

<div class="sb">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<div class="rp">Pertaining to the above:</div>

<p class="p">
Also, the <span class="kt">four cups of wine</span> are likewise in the aspect of the <span class="kt">ascent of the holy <em>Malchus</em></span> from within the aspect of concealment. As Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote: the four cups correspond to four mitzvos that apply on every Yom Tov, corresponding to the aspect of <em>Malchus</em>, which is the number four, ascending on Yom Tov from the four kingdoms. Therefore, they are <span class="kt">four cups of wine</span>, in the aspect of <span class="sq">"wine enters, a secret goes out"</span> — that is, the concealment is revealed, for the holiness had been enclothed there in great secrecy and hiddenness, as mentioned above. Furthermore, there within the concealments, specifically exalted holiness is enclothed — the aspect of the <span class="kt">secrets of the Torah</span>, as mentioned above. Through the wine, this is revealed — the aspect of <span class="sq">"wine enters, a secret goes out"</span> — and through this, <em>Malchus</em> ascends, which is the aspect of the number four, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of the four cups of wine.
</p>

<div class="sb">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<div class="rp">Pertaining to the Sefirah:</div>

<p class="p">
And this is what is brought in the writings of the Ari z"l: <span class="kt"><em>LaOmer</em></span> in <em>gematria</em> equals <span class="kt"><em>Shem</em></span> (Name). For through the aspect of <em>Sefiras HaOmer</em> — counting "today is day one <em>LaOmer</em>," etc. — through this, one makes the aspect of a <span class="kt">Name</span>, which is the aspect of attributes and days, as mentioned above, which is the essential rectification of holiness, as mentioned above. And therefore, the attributes of Hashem, blessed be He, as it were, are called <span class="kt"><em>Sefiros</em></span> — for this is the essential rectification: that they are in the aspect of <em>Sefiros</em>, that is, attributes — that they are, as it were, numbered and counted and measured in the aspect of vessels, the aspect of measure and weight and number, which is the essential rectification, as mentioned above and as is brought.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>Omer</em> of barley</span>, from which the days of the counting begin. An <em>Omer</em> is a <span class="kt">measure</span> — the aspect of attributes and vessels, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="kt"><em>Omer</em> of barley (<em>s'orim</em>)</span> — the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>shi'urim</em></span> (measurements), the aspect of the attributes, which are the aspect of <span class="sq"><em>shi'urin d'liba</em></span> — "measurements of the heart" — through which one grasps Him, blessed be He, as it were, in the aspect of <span class="v">"Her husband is known in the gates (<em>sh'arim</em>)"</span> <span class="vs">(Mishlai 31:23)</span> — <span class="sq">"each one according to what he measures in his heart"</span> — which are the aspect of the attributes and <em>Sefiros</em> that are comprised in the heart, as is known. For the heart is the <span class="kt">painter of the attributes</span>, as Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote. And they are the aspect of <em>shi'urin d'liba</em>, through which specifically the completeness of <em>daas</em> is achieved — for through this one grasps Him, blessed be He, as it were. And this is the aspect of <em>Omer s'orim</em> — the aspect of <span class="v">"Her husband is known in the gates (<em>sh'arim</em>)"</span> — the essential rectification in the aspect of measurements and vessels and attributes, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, then the counting begins, which is the aspect of the rectification of the vessels and attributes, as mentioned above. And all this is the rectification of <em>daas</em>, as is explained there in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span> — that through the Torah, which is the aspect of His Name, blessed be He — the aspect of vessels and attributes — through this, one calls Him, blessed be He, and draws vitality from the Life of all life — that is, <em>daas</em>. And this is the aspect of <span class="v">"Her husband is known in the gates"</span> mentioned above — that one merits to know Him, blessed be He, through <em>shi'urin d'liba</em>, which is the aspect of <em>Omer s'orim</em>, the aspect of vessels and attributes, the aspect of <em>Shem</em>, the aspect of <em>Sefiras HaOmer</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is why the custom is to <span class="kt">let the hair grow during the days of the <em>Sefirah</em></span>. For the hairs are the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>tzimtzumim</em> and measurements</span> through which the light of the brain and <em>daas</em> is contracted — so that it should be possible to grasp Him, blessed be He, as is brought in the discourse <span class="v">"Maishra d'sakina"</span> <span class="vs">(Siman 30)</span>. Therefore, during the days of the <em>Sefirah</em>, we let the hair grow — for then the rectification is in the aspect of hairs, the aspect of <em>Omer s'orim</em>, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, on the <span class="kt">first day of the <em>Sefirah</em></span> — that is, on the day of the offering of the <em>Omer</em> of barley — was the <span class="kt">downfall of Haman</span>. For through the aspect of the Name, the aspect of the rectification of the vessels and attributes, which is the rectification of <em>daas</em> as mentioned above — through this, one reveals the concealment and the holy <em>Malchus</em> is revealed, in the aspect of <span class="kt">Esther</span>, who was at first in concealment, the aspect of <span class="v">"I will surely hide"</span> (<em>haster astir</em>). And this was accomplished through the aspect of <span class="kt">Mordechai</span>, who is the aspect of the rectification of the holy <em>Malchus</em> — the aspect of the <em>Omer</em> of barley, which is the aspect of Mordechai and Esther, as Rabeinu, may his light shine, wrote in the discourse <span class="v">"V'aileh hamishpatim — b'lu'ai d'Korach"</span> <span class="vs">(see there, Siman 10)</span>. Therefore, then is the subjugation of the wicked kingdom — the downfall of Haman-Amalek — which is subdued through the aspect of the rectification of the Name through the aspect of the <em>Omer</em> of barley, as mentioned above. And as is explained there in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span>; see there. For the downfall of Amalek depends on the aspect of the rectification and completeness of His Name, blessed be He, as it is written: <span class="sq">"His Name is not complete"</span> etc. — <span class="sq">"until his memory is erased"</span> — for this depends on that, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, then — on the day of the waving of the <em>Omer</em> — was also the <span class="kt">downfall of many great nations</span>, all of whom are in the aspect of the wicked kingdom that is subdued through the rectification of the holy <em>Malchus</em> through the aspect of the <em>Omer</em> of barley, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is why the <span class="kt"><em>Omer</em> permits the new crop</span>. For then one merits to eat bread in the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>man</em></span> (manna), the aspect of <span class="kt">bread from heaven</span> — which one merits through the revelation of <em>daas</em>, through the revelation of the concealment, through the subjugation of the kingdom of Haman-Amalek — and this is accomplished through the rectification of the <em>Omer</em> of barley, which is the aspect of the totality of the Torah, the aspect of the <em>Sh'ma d'Kudsha B'rich Hu</em>, as mentioned above. (See all this in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span> mentioned above.)
</p>

<p class="p">
For the <span class="kt">eating of Yisrael is holy</span>, and in particular the <span class="kt">bread</span> — that is, the <span class="kt">five species of grain</span> — which are the essential food and satiation and the essential vitality, for in them the <em>daas</em> is enclothed, which is the vitality. Therefore, they are five — the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>Hei</em> of <em>daas</em></span> — as is brought above in <span class="vs">Hilchos N'tilas Yadayim</span>. Therefore, they need rectification — for wherever there is greater vitality and holiness, there is a <em>k'lipah</em> (shell) that precedes the fruit. Therefore, the bread from the five species of grain requires many rectifications, which are the <span class="kt">ten mitzvos pertaining to bread</span>.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, one must rectify the new grain through the <em>Omer</em>. For through the rectification of the <em>Omer</em> of barley as mentioned above, the <em>daas</em> is revealed. And then one merits the aspect of <em>man</em>, the aspect of bread from heaven — that is, the bread and grain of Yisrael becomes in the aspect of <em>man</em>, etc. For the <em>daas</em> and vitality are revealed — for the wicked kingdom is subdued, the <em>k'lipah</em> that precedes the fruit — through the rectification of the <em>Omer</em> of barley, as mentioned above. And then they are fit for the <span class="kt">receiving of the Torah</span> — for the Torah was given only to <span class="sq">the eaters of the <em>man</em></span>. Therefore, one must rectify the bread of Yisrael in the aspect of <em>man</em> through the <em>Omer</em>, as mentioned above. And then one merits the receiving of the Torah on Shavuos — for the entire rectification of the <em>Omer</em> and the counting is for the sake of receiving the Torah. For from this itself, the Torah is formed.
</p>

<p class="p">
That is: as is explained there in the discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span> mentioned above — that through revealing the concealment within concealment, through this, exceedingly lofty Torah is revealed, for specifically there, exceedingly lofty Torah was enclothed — the <span class="kt">mysteries of the Torah</span>. And this is the aspect of <span class="v">"The wealth he swallowed, he shall vomit up"</span> <span class="vs">(Iyov 20:15)</span> — that one extracts from the wicked kingdom — which is the kingdom of Amalek — all the sparks, and from this, <span class="kt">Torah</span> is formed, which is the aspect of <span class="kt"><em>Aishes Chayil</em></span> (a Woman of Valor), etc.; see there.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt">Torah that is received on Shavuos</span>, which is the fiftieth day of the <em>Omer</em>. That is: through the <em>Omer</em> and the counting — through which the kingdom of Amalek is subdued as mentioned above — then the Torah that was hidden there in the aspect of concealment within concealment is revealed, and one merits to grasp it on Shavuos. This is the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>Minchah Chadashah</em></span> — the <span class="kt">two loaves of wheat</span> that are offered on Shavuos. <em>Minchah chadashah</em> — this is the aspect of the <span class="kt">new Torah</span> that is formed through the revelation of the concealment, etc., as mentioned above. As Rabeinu, may his light shine, explained there, on the verse <span class="vs">(Bamidbar 28:26)</span>: <span class="v">"And on the day of the first-fruits, when you bring a new meal-offering to Hashem, on your Shavuos"</span>; see there.
</p>

<p class="p">
And similarly, it is found in the <em>Ra'aya M'heimna</em> that the <em>Omer</em> is the aspect of the <span class="kt">revealed Torah</span>, and the two loaves are the aspect of the <span class="kt">hidden Torah</span>. That is: the <em>Omer</em> is the aspect of the revealed Torah, through which one reveals the concealment, etc. And then exceedingly lofty Torah is revealed — the mysteries of the Torah — the aspect of <em>Minchah chadashah</em>, the aspect of the Torah that is received on Shavuos, which is the <span class="kt">fiftieth day</span> — the aspect of the <span class="kt">supernal gate, the gate of <em>Nun</em></span> (the fiftieth gate), as is explained there.
</p>

<p class="p">
Therefore, the <span class="kt">war with Amalek was before the Giving of the Torah</span>. And likewise, <em>Parshas Amalek</em> is juxtaposed to <em>Parshas Yisro</em>, which is the receiving of the Torah. For the essential Torah is revealed through the downfall of Amalek, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is the aspect of the <span class="kt">seven weeks that we count</span>. For there are two concealments — concealment and concealment within concealment — as is explained there. And they correspond to two aspects of Torah: the <span class="kt">revealed and the hidden</span> — <em>razin</em> and <em>razin d'razin</em> (secrets and secrets of secrets). For within the concealment within concealment, specifically the mysteries of the Torah are enclothed, as mentioned above. Therefore, one must rectify and reveal both concealments, to reveal both aspects of the Torah. And their rectification is through the rectification of the days and attributes as mentioned above, which are seven days, as is known. And it is known that there are <span class="kt">seven supernal days</span>, which are the seven Shabbasos, as is found in the Holy Zohar — and they are in <span class="kt"><em>Binah</em></span> (Understanding), which is the aspect of the mysteries of the Torah, which is the aspect of Shavuos — the fiftieth day, the aspect of the <span class="kt">fifty gates of <em>Binah</em></span>. Therefore, one must count seven Shabbasos to rectify the seven supernal days, to reveal the concealment within concealment — through which one merits the mysteries of the Torah, the aspect of the fifty gates of <em>Binah</em>, the aspect of Shavuos, the aspect of <em>man</em>, as mentioned above and as is explained there; see the entire discourse <span class="v">"Uv'yom habikurim"</span> well.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is what our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="sq">Haman said: "Your <em>Omer</em> came and conquered my ten thousand talents of silver."</span> <span class="kt">"Silver" specifically.</span> For the essential strengthening of Haman was through the ten thousand talents of <span class="kt">silver</span> — that is, he gathered great wealth in which were all the holy sparks, as is explained there. And this is what is written <span class="vs">(Esther 3:9)</span>: <span class="v">"And ten thousand talents of silver I will weigh"</span> etc. <span class="v">"into the treasuries of the king — against the Jews"</span> etc. That is: he sought to give power to the wicked kingdom through the silver he gathered, as mentioned above. But through the <em>Omer</em>, which is the aspect of the Torah, the aspect of the <em>Sh'ma d'Kudsha B'rich Hu</em> — through which one reveals the concealment — through this, the wicked kingdom is subdued. And then the power of the wealth is subdued, for all the sparks are extracted from it, in the aspect of <span class="v">"The wealth he swallowed, he shall vomit up,"</span> as mentioned above. And this is what [Haman] said: that the <em>Omer</em> conquered the ten thousand talents of silver — the power of the wealth, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And this is why the <em>Omer</em> is offered on the <span class="kt">16th of Nissan</span>, whose <em>gematria</em> equals the <span class="kt">Name that emerges from the initial letters</span> of the aforementioned verse: <span class="v"><em><b>Ch</b>ayil <b>b</b>ala <b>v</b>ay'ki'enu</em></span>, as mentioned above. And as is written in the <em>Ra'aya M'heimna</em>: <span class="sq">"Through the offering of the <em>Omer</em>, the <em>Sitra Achra</em> flees from <em>Aishes Chayil</em>"</span> — for through the <em>Omer</em>, one extracts the holy sparks from the wicked kingdom — Haman-Amalek — in the aspect of <span class="v">"The wealth he swallowed, he shall vomit up,"</span> and Torah is formed from this, which is <em>Aishes Chayil</em>, as mentioned above — the Torah that is received on Shavuos, the aspect of <em>Minchah chadashah</em>, as mentioned above. (See the <em>Ra'aya M'heimna</em> there.)
</p>

<p class="p">
And similarly at the <span class="kt">Splitting of the Sea</span>, when Yisrael plundered the Egyptians of great wealth — it is stated that Yisrael then merited a very great <span class="kt">spiritual perception</span>. For this depends on that: through extracting the wealth from the wicked kingdom, they merited lofty Torah — for then <em>Aishes Chayil</em> is formed from this, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And similarly, regarding the <span class="kt">final redemption</span>, it is said <span class="vs">(Yeshayahu 23:18)</span>: <span class="v">"And her merchandise and her hire shall be holy to Hashem"</span> etc. — <span class="v">"for those who sit before Hashem shall her merchandise be, and for a covering of the ancient (<em>atik</em>)"</span> — <span class="sq">"these are the things that He concealed,"</span> etc. That is: through the wealth of the wicked kingdom that will return to Yisrael, through this very thing they will merit the <span class="kt">mysteries of the Torah</span>, as mentioned above — which is the aspect of <span class="sq">"a covering of the ancient — these are the things that He concealed"</span> — the aspect of the <span class="kt"><em>Torah of the <em>Atika</em></em></span> that will be revealed in the future, speedily in our days, amen.
</p>

<div class="sb">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<p class="p">
The <em>Poskim</em> gave the <span class="kt">mnemonic <em>PeLaG</em></span>: that the day on which Purim falls, <span class="kt">Lag BaOmer</span> falls [on the same day of the week], as is written in the <em>Shulchan Aruch</em>. For <span class="kt">Purim</span> and <em>Sefiras HaOmer</em> are in the <span class="kt">same aspect</span>. And the perception of Torah on the fiftieth day — Shavuos — comes through the aspect of Purim, through the downfall of Haman-Amalek, as mentioned above. And <span class="kt">Lag BaOmer</span> is also a day of the perception of Torah within the days of the <em>Sefirah</em> — for it is the <span class="kt"><em>Hillula Rabba</em> of Rabbi Shimon bar Yochai</span>, who perceived then what he perceived. Therefore, it falls on the day that Purim falls — for the perception of the <em>Sefirah</em> is through the aspect of Purim, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="kt">Lag BaOmer</span> — the aspect of <span class="v">"Uncover my eyes, that I may behold wonders from Your Torah"</span> <span class="vs">(Tehillim 119:18)</span> — the aspect of the perception that one attains then, as mentioned above.
</p>

<p class="p">
And therefore, <span class="kt">Haman is alluded to in <em>Parshas HaMan</em></span> (the portion about the manna), as it is written <span class="vs">(Shemos 16:35)</span>: <span class="v">"<em>Es haman</em> (the manna) they ate."</span> That is: the <em>man</em> (manna) is formed from the aspect of the subjugation of the kingdom of <span class="kt">Haman</span>-Amalek, as mentioned above. And therefore, <span class="sq">"the letters of this one are as the letters of that one"</span> — for from Haman, the <em>man</em> is formed, as mentioned above.
</p>

<div class="sb">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<div class="rp">Pertaining to Hilchos Rosh Chodesh above:</div>

<p class="p">
<span class="v">"And of the children of Yissachar, those who had understanding of the times, to know what Yisrael should do"</span> <span class="vs">(Divrai HaYamim I, 12:33)</span> — they were expert in the <span class="kt">secret of the intercalation</span>, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said regarding this verse. And this is: <span class="v">"those who had understanding of the <em>times</em>"</span> — they knew how to <span class="kt">draw <em>Binah</em> and <em>Chochmah</em> into the <em>times</em></span> — that is, the days and attributes, as mentioned above. And this is: <span class="v">"to know what Yisrael should <em>do</em>"</span> — they knew how to <span class="kt">make <em>mah</em></span> — that is, Torah, in the aspect of <span class="sq"><em>"u'mah yai'aseh bah"</em></span>, as mentioned above and as is explained in the aforementioned discourse. That is: to reveal the <em>daas</em> and the Torah from within the concealment — to make Torah from the concealment, which is the aspect of <em>mah</em>. And all this through the aspect of <span class="v">"those who had understanding of the times"</span> — through drawing wisdom from the Life of all life into the times and days, through which one reveals the concealment, as mentioned above. And therefore, our Sages, of blessed memory, derived from this that they were expert in the <span class="kt">secret of the intercalation</span>. For <em>Kiddush HaChodesh</em> is accomplished through this aspect — through the revelation of the concealment, as mentioned above.
</p>


<div class="ts">
<div class="th">Thematic Summary · Hilchos Pesach</div>
<p>The entire structure of the Pesach night and the <em>Sefirah</em> period embodies the principle of revealing <em>daas</em> from within concealment. Shabbos HaGadol is the source from which the redemption of Pesach draws its power. The three <em>matzos</em> become four through breaking — symbolizing the completion of <em>Malchus</em> in its four camps. The son's questions are holy <em>machlokes</em>, the creative "dispute" that mirrors the initial <em>tzimtzum</em> necessary for creation. The Haggadah's cries and sighs purify the "heavens" — the hands — from which one receives speech. <em>Karpas</em> alludes both to teshuvah (the green vegetable) and to the <em>K'sones Passim</em> whose blemished <em>machlokes</em> is now rectified. The <em>Afikoman</em> — hidden and then revealed — is the taste of <em>man</em> that emerges once the holy dispute is complete. The counting of the <em>Omer</em> creates vessels and attributes to receive light in measure, and the <em>Omer</em> offering itself subdues Amalek and permits the new grain. Shavuos — the fiftieth gate — reveals the hidden Torah that was enclothed in the deepest concealment. The mnemonic PeLaG links Purim and Lag BaOmer: both are moments when Torah perception breaks through the concealment of the wicked kingdom.</p>
</div>

